 "pdCallTexts": [
  {
   "deadId": "gen_5activj",
   "entryDay": 42,
   "cause": "the expedition",
   "lines": [
    "d42: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Felicia Diaz is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d42: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d42: 🕯️ Felicia Diaz is dead — the expedition. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d42: What Felicia kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d42: \"Felicia's gone.\" Dwayne looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Felicia.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d42: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Trong blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d42: 📖 LEARNED: Tireless Stride (Level 1). You walk like water downhill — no wasted steps, no wasted breath. Every mile costs 15% less.",
    "d42: The warm hum behind your ribs is gone. The reactor went with Felicia's body — it does not come out, and it does not pass on. Hunger is back on the table. (One reactor per world, and the world already spent its one.)",
    "d42: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d42: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Felicia Diaz, 42 days. The mantle passes to Trong Binh.",
    "d42: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Trong Binh, 69 — a postal worker. Their hands know different work now: Beast-calm, Bloodhound.",
    "d42: The village's quarrel was with Felicia — and Felicia is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d42: At the grave, Dwayne, Rewi, Somchai and 4 more speak for Trong — \"Felicia trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d42: The fire knew Trong before the Codex did — their name already carried weight here."
